app "skyline bay" {
  meta { owl: 23; description: "A 3D island city builder: lay roads, zone homes, shops and industry, bring power and water, add services and parks, and grow a hamlet into a skyline"; version: "1.12"; license: "MIT"; category: "games" }
  // How it works. The island is 22 x 22 tiles, kept in two persisted lists: g (what's on a tile) and lv (how far a
  // zoned lot has grown, 0 to 3). Every 2 seconds a tick settles the cash, and lots with demand for their zone grow a
  // level if what they need is there: a road that reaches the highway, power, water (from level 2), land value
  // (parks, plazas, a sea view, services nearby, no industry next door) and the city's level. The city levels up with
  // its population, which unlocks buildings; quests lead the way and pay out.
  //
  // Drawing: everything is 3D (Canvas scene and model). The sea is one big plane, the island one terrain whose cells
  // take the tiles' colors, the road markings and bridge decks a few meshes of flat quads, each in a scene of its own so
  // nothing on the ground is sorted under it. Buildings are meshes made once from boxes, gabled and hipped roofs,
  // cylinders and cones, and each tile draws one with model(), turned to face its road. Cars drive routes walked along
  // the roads; boats sail the bay; chimneys smoke. The buildings' scene reads no clock, so the launcher keeps it drawn
  // and only works through its triangles again when the city or the view changes; what moves has scenes of its own,
  // cars and boats under it and smoke, rockets and lots rising over it. One finger pans (or paints roads and zones while
  // a tool is out), two fingers zoom and turn the island, and a tap builds or looks at a tile.
  //
  // Power is the sun's: solar farms make it while it shines, and every 4 minutes (by the clock, so it carries on while
  // closed) clouds roll in for about a minute and a half and the farms make little. Batteries store what's left over
  // for the clouds, and a city without enough goes dark: dark buildings pay no taxes and can't grow. A research lab buys better panels and batteries, and in the end rocketry, for a
  // launch pad that sends satellites up for paying customers.
  //
  // Traffic: a lot's traffic is the buildings around it (5 x 5 tiles, by level) over the roads around it, so dense
  // blocks with few roads jam, which costs land value and happiness. Bus stops (with a depot running the buses) ease it
  // by 35% 3 tiles round, and subway stations by 60% 4 tiles round once tunnels link them to another station. Tunnels
  // are a layer of their own, `sub`, dug like roads and seen in the subway view; bus stops another, `stops`, the road
  // tiles with a shelter on their sidewalk.
  //
  // Land: a city's island has a coast of its own (cities from before stay square), cut into 16 parcels of 5 or 6 tiles
  // a side (9 on the smaller islands from before). A new city owns the middle and the highway's side; the rest is bought
  // a parcel at a time, beside what's owned, each dearer than the last. (The island stays 22 x 22 tiles: every tile is
  // worked through on each change, and a bigger grid would run out of the launcher's work per update.)
  //
  // Cities: up to four, on four maps (a bay, a forest lake, a harbor, a river delta), easy to hard. The city being played
  // is in the states above; the others wait in `saves` with their cash and the time they were left, so they get
  // the same small bonus as a closed app, and swapping one in swaps the playing one out.
  title: ""
  statusBar: false
  edge: true
  // smooth under the finger (an app at 60 keeps full rate), easier on the battery while watching
  fps: gm != 0 ? 60 : modes.saver ? 15 : 30
  source modes = android.modes
  icon: """<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 256 256">
    <clipPath id="t"><rect width="256" height="256" rx="56"/></clipPath>
    <g clip-path="url(#t)">
    <linearGradient id="sky" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#7fd0f5"/><stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#3f9fd8"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#2f86c4"/></linearGradient>
    <rect width="256" height="256" fill="url(#sky)"/>
    <circle cx="222" cy="34" r="20" fill="#ffd56a"/>
    <path d="M-27.8 160.0 L128.0 237.9 L128.0 253.9 L-27.8 176.0 Z" fill="#d9bf82"/>
    <path d="M283.8 160.0 L128.0 237.9 L128.0 253.9 L283.8 176.0 Z" fill="#c4a86a"/>
    <path d="M128.0 82.1 L283.8 160.0 L128.0 237.9 L-27.8 160.0 Z" fill="#f2e1ab"/>
    <path d="M128.0 90.8 L266.3 160.0 L128.0 229.2 L-10.3 160.0 Z" fill="#8bcd65"/>
    <path d="M96.8 213.6 L128.0 229.2 L159.2 213.6 L128.0 218.9 Z" fill="#4fb0dd"/>
